# Draft kk: Narrow render encoder end barriers behind MESA_KK_BARRIERS=narrow
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46524 state=closed
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

```
kk: Narrow render encoder end barriers behind

Every KosmicKrisp encoder currently ends with an ALL to ALL barrier, preventing vertex work of the next render pass from overlapping fragment work of the previous one.

Behind MESA_KK_BARRIERS=narrow (off by default), render encoders that drew without meta passes or visibility results end with beforeStages = ALL & ~(VERTEX | OBJECT | MESH). Vulkan pipeline barriers, vkCmdWaitEvents2, and vertex-stage timestamp writes record fragment-to-vertex and vertex-to-vertex dependencies and enforce them as consumer barriers at render encoder start (or in-place / by splitting an open render encoder). Recorded waits stay sticky across encoders until a compute encoder that ran a direct non-zero dispatch ends with ALL to ALL.

MESA_KK_BARRIER_LOG=1 logs narrow-barrier counters via mesa_logi.

Testing (Apple M5 Pro, macOS 27.2, MESA_KK_BARRIERS=narrow):

dEQP-VK: 0 new failures against the base on sync (2,229), paths (1,456), standing (79,312), and non-sparse (449,481) case lists; power (178,121) hit 1 flaky case (non_zero_vertex_instance_indirect_draw, passed 5/5 on retry).
Valid-Vulkan trigger check (vkCmdDispatch -> render pass -> vkCmdPipelineBarrier2 split -> vkCmdWriteTimestamp2(VERTEX)): verified in-place, split, and vertex-timestamp consumer paths.
Metal transitive ordering through a non-empty compute encoder (narrow render end -> compute -> render vertex without consumer): 0 misses in 297 rounds at 800, 2000, and 8000 writer iterations.

Assisted-by: LLM
